From da5ff31e0aa049dc6c36eb4b6fb34634b1dc30e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [TEST PATCH] dbus: reacquire USB device on Resume

Sanctuary reproduces an S4 failure where the sensor re-enumerates after
hibernate but python-validity retains the pre-hibernate PyUSB device handle.
The existing Resume method calls init.open_common(), which assumes usb.dev
already refers to a usable device. After S4, operations through that object
fail with USBError ENODEV.

For the default single-device path, call init.open() instead. This runs
usb.open() before open_common() and therefore reacquires the re-enumerated
sensor.

This test patch deliberately does not claim correct --devpath behaviour yet.
That path needs separate treatment because USB bus/address may change across
re-enumeration.
---
 dbus_service/dbus-service | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dbus_service/dbus-service b/dbus_service/dbus-service
index 1c63e8d..0000000 100755
--- a/dbus_service/dbus-service
+++ b/dbus_service/dbus-service
@@ -70,9 +70,9 @@ class Device(dbus.service.Object):
     def Resume(self):
         logging.debug('In Resume')
         tls.reset()
         try:
-            init.open_common()
+            init.open()
         except:
-            init.open_common()
+            init.open()
 
     @dbus.service.method(dbus_interface=INTERFACE_NAME, in_signature="s", out_signature="as")
     def ListEnrolledFingers(self, user):
-- 
